validation.json
    proseweave's own validation results (see validation/).

judged_models.json
    proseweave's own fitted weights for the judgement-scale properties
    (judged.py): ridge coefficients and feature scalings, fitted on the
    validation corpora's reference values. Numbers only; no text is stored.
    MIT, like the code.

syntax_en.bin.gz
    Learned weights of proseweave's text pipeline (syntax.py): a two-pass
    part-of-speech tagger, sentence segmenter, dependency parser and
    coarse-class model, with a tag dictionary and short lists of lemma
    corrections and tokenizer exceptions. Feature weights only; no running
    text is stored. Details: data/SYNTAX_LICENSE.md. Build scripts:
    tools/syntax/.

    Licence: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/).
    The weights were learned from automatic parses of the following texts:

      - Universal Dependencies English Web Treebank (UD_English-EWT), raw
        sentences. CC BY-SA 4.0. Attribution: Silveira et al. (2014), "A Gold
        Standard Dependency Corpus for English", and the Universal Dependencies
        contributors.
      - English Wikipedia, randomly sampled articles (plain-text extracts,
        2026-09). CC BY-SA 4.0. Attribution: Wikipedia contributors.
      - English Wikinews, randomly sampled articles (2026-09). CC BY 2.5.
        Attribution: Wikinews contributors.
      - Project Gutenberg books, public domain in the United States. No
        Project Gutenberg header, licence text or trademark is used or
        reproduced.

    The parses used as training labels were made at build time by spaCy's
    en_core_web_sm 3.7 model, which is distributed under the MIT licence
    (Copyright (C) 2016-2024 ExplosionAI GmbH, 2016 spaCy GmbH, 2015 Matthew
    Honnibal; licence text as for stop_words_en.txt above). No part of the
    spaCy model is included in the file.

    The sentence segmenter's weights were additionally learned from spaCy
    en_core_web_sm annotations of open web text: Common Pile v0.1
    news_filtered articles marked CC BY 4.0 (CC BY-SA articles skipped),
    Foodista (CC BY 3.0) and English Wikinews (CC BY 2.5). Build script:
    tools/syntax/train_seg2.py (data: tools/dump_news.py).

syllables_en.bin.gz, stress_en.bin.gz
    Syllable counts per word (the number of vowel phonemes in the first listed
    pronunciation) and, for words not stressed on their first syllable, which
    syllables carry primary stress, derived from the Carnegie Mellon Pronouncing Dictionary
    0.7a, as distributed in the NLTK data package, in proseweave's packed table
    format. Build scripts: tools/build_syllables.py, tools/pack_tables.py.
    Full upstream notice: data/LICENSE_syllables.md.

